[31m+         "blocks": [[39m
[31m+           {[39m
[31m+             "text": "Extracted feature vectors are standardized and passed to a Support Vector Machine with a Radial Basis Function (RBF) kernel. To provide meaningful risk scores rather than binary decisions, the classifier applies Platt scaling via probability calibration.",[39m
[31m+             "type": "paragraph",[39m
[31m+           },[39m
[31m+           {[39m
[31m+             "text": "Trained scaler and model artifacts are serialized using joblib, enabling instant local CPU inference with zero external API dependencies or network latency.",[39m
[31m+             "type": "paragraph",[39m
[31m+           },[39m
[31m+         ],[39m
[31m+         "heading": "Classifier Training and Probability Calibration",[39m
[31m+         "id": "model-architecture",[39m
[31m+       },[39m
[31m+       {[39m
[31m+         "blocks": [[39m
[31m+           {[39m
[31m+             "text": "On a deterministic 80/20 train/test evaluation split, the calibrated model demonstrated 78.5% held-out test accuracy across test sets.",[39m
[31m+             "type": "paragraph",[39m
[31m+           },[39m
[31m+           {[39m
[31m+             "items": [[39m
[31m+               "Heavy JPEG re-compression degrades high-frequency LBP micro-textures, reducing detection confidence.",[39m
[31m+               "Handcrafted texture features remain sensitive to input scaling; images should be evaluated at native or standardized resolutions.",[39m
